  "Question": "A triangle has vertices \\(A(0,0)\\), \\(B(4,0)\\), and \\(C(0,3)\\). What is the length of side \\(BC\\)?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "5",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "To find \\(BC\\), take the magnitude of the vector from \\(B\\) to \\(C\\). Subtracting the coordinates of \\(B\\) from those of \\(C\\) gives \\(\\overrightarrow{BC}=(0-4,3-0)=(-4,3)\\), whose magnitude is \\(\\sqrt{16+9}=5\\). Thus \\(BC=5\\).",
